&lt;h1&gt;Direct Hire Recruiter (Full Desk/360)&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Please Note:&lt;/strong&gt; While this role is remote, candidates must live within the Atlanta, Charlotte, Raleigh, Dallas, or Houston metro areas. Applications from candidates outside of these markets cannot be considered.*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Openwork, we&#39;re looking for experienced agency recruiters who know how to build and run a successful full desk. This is not a recruiting coordinator, sourcer, or recruiting-only role. We are seeking proven 360 recruiters with a track record of developing client relationships, generating job orders, recruiting talent, and making placements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As am Executive/Direct Hire Recruiter, you&#39;ll own the entire business cycle from business development and client management to candidate recruitment and placement. You&#39;ll have the autonomy to build your market, grow your book of business, and directly impact your earnings and career growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be successful in this role, you must have at least 3-5+ years of experience running a true full desk within a professional staffing environment.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow your own book of business through proactive business development activities, networking, referrals, and strategic outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a full 360 recruiting desk, owning both client acquisition and candidate delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect, cold call, conduct client meetings, and uncover hiring opportunities within your market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build long-term partnerships with hiring managers and decision-makers by understanding their business challenges and providing talent solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill-market top candidates to generate new business opportunities and create demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, interview, assess, and present high-caliber professional talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full hiring process, including candidate sourcing, qualification, interview preparation, offer negotiation, and placement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain ongoing relationships with both clients and placed candidates to drive retention, referrals, and repeat business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently achieve recruiting, sales, activity, and revenue goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate ATS documentation and pipeline management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5+ years of experience running a true full desk (360) within a professional staffing or recruiting agency environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success generating new business and managing client relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of recruiting and placing professional-level talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing the entire recruitment lifecycle from business development through placement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable making outbound sales calls, conducting client meetings, negotiating fees, and closing business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consultative selling, relationship-building, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while managing multiple searches, clients, and priorities simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
